# Apple Root CA ("Apple Inc. Root Certificate", self-signed, valid
# 2006-04-25 to 2035-02-09). Published at
# https://www.apple.com/certificateauthority/ (first entry under "Apple
# Root Certificates") and also at https://www.apple.com/appleca/AppleIncRootCertificate.cer
#
# Needed because gdmf.apple.com (Settings > OS Lifecycle's Apple GDMF
# fetch, backend/src/modules/catalogs/gdmfCatalog.ts) serves a chain that
# terminates in this root, and it isn't part of Alpine's default
# ca-certificates bundle (nor Node's own compiled-in CA list, which is
# Mozilla-derived and doesn't include Apple's internal PKI). Without it,
# every fetch fails with "self-signed certificate in certificate chain" —
# confirmed against the actual chain Apple serves:
#   0 gdmf.apple.com                    (leaf)
#   1 Apple Server Authentication CA    (intermediate)
#   2 Apple Root CA                     (self-signed root — this file)
#
# Loaded via NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS (see Dockerfile) rather than
# update-ca-certificates, since Node.js ignores the OS trust store by
# default and uses its own bundled CA list — NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS is the
# supported way to extend that list without patching Node itself or
# disabling verification globally (NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0 would
# have also silenced this, but at the cost of no longer verifying *any*
# outbound HTTPS call this process makes, including ones carrying the
# Applivery API bearer token).
